	order_index: 0
	quest_links: [ ]
	quests: [
		{
			dependencies: ["15ACD993630984F4"]
			description: [
				"Now, I'm sure in your travels you've come across some items with rather unique properties. Found in chests or dropped by mobs, these special properties are known as &6&oAffixes&r."
				"Affixes come in various categories, each with many possible effects. &o&6Stat Affixes&r change attributes such as speed or health; &6&oDurability Affixes&r decrease the damage taken by an item, often through negating it; &o&6Effect Affixes&r give a wide range of unique abilities such as applying a potion effect when striking an enemy or making the attack AOE; and both &o&6Gem Sockets and Augment Sockets&r give you slots to put gems and augments into, but more on that later."
				"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/affixes.png width:237 height:135 align:center}"
			]
			hide_until_deps_complete: true
			id: "2B712988FC2E66C0"
			rewards: [{
				amount: 100L
				currency: "eternalcurrencies:ancientcoins"
				id: "2E6D8F4855ACFAF9"
				ignore_reward_blocking: true
				type: "eternalcurrencies:currency"
			}]
			tasks: [{
				advancement: "apotheosis:affix/root"
				criterion: ""
				id: "75CF3FBF11F04074"
				title: "Find An Item With An Affix"
				type: "advancement"
			}]
			title: "Affix To This"
			x: 0.0d
			y: -1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["15ACD993630984F4"]
			description: [
				"Affixes will certainly not be the only item you come across in your travles. What is that shine in the dungeon's chest? The shimmering from within your enemy's bag? Why, it a &o&6Gem&r of course."
				"Gems are items that can add various effects to items they are slotted into. They can be found in several states, each with a corresponding rarity. These are &8Cracked&r, &2Chipped&r, &9Flawed&r, &5Normal&r, &cFlawless&r, and &6Perfect&r."
				"&6&oNot all gems work with all item types.&r You may find one that can only be used on armor, or perhaps everything but swords. In addition, &6&omost slots you'll find on Affixed items will be tiered&r, and will only accept a gem &6&oof the same or lower rarity&r."
				"If all of these match, then inserting the gem is as simple as putting both the item and the gem inside a &o&6smithing table&r."
				"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/gems.png width:237 height:135 align:center}"
			]
			hide_until_deps_complete: true
			id: "5A97C15CA4463102"
			rewards: [{
				amount: 100L
				currency: "eternalcurrencies:ancientcoins"
				id: "190603B06A75A6E6"
				ignore_reward_blocking: true
				type: "eternalcurrencies:currency"
			}]
			tasks: [{
				advancement: "apotheosis:affix/gem"
				criterion: ""
				id: "5FE6842CCC27A043"
				title: "Find a Gem"
				type: "advancement"
			}]
			title: "Shine Bright"
			x: -2.0d
			y: -1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["15ACD993630984F4"]
			description: [
				"Not all mobs are made equal. For some, power has been grasped in some way. These are &o&6Bosses&r. Stronger variants of mobs wielding special equipment unique to them."
				"Most often, you'll come across these variants when one &o&6invades your world&r, shown through a sound playing alongside text notifying you and a beacon of light illuminating them from afar. "
				"You may also come across &o&6Mini Bosses&r while exploring, rare wandering mobs who have tapped into the power of Affixes."
				"Finally, they speak of &6&odungeons&r hidden under the dirt and rock of the world, treasure and knowledge stored away, guarded by a Boss."
				"When slain, a Boss will always drop &6&oits unique Affixed item&r. These are typically stronger than most other affixed items you'll come across. And as a memento of the one who held it before you, the boss's name with be added to the item."
				"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/bosses.png width:237 height:135 align:center}"
			]
			hide_until_deps_complete: true
			id: "25927B5C8F23FCEA"
			rewards: [{
				amount: 100L
				currency: "eternalcurrencies:ancientcoins"
				id: "296C9C7C8A69DFC1"
				ignore_reward_blocking: true
				type: "eternalcurrencies:currency"
			}]
			shape: "hexagon"
			tasks: [{
				advancement: "apotheosis:affix/boss"
				criterion: ""
				icon: {
					Count: 1
					id: "ftbquests:custom_icon"
					tag: {
						Icon: "cataclysm:textures/gui/boss_bar/life_remain_skull.png"
					}
				}
				id: "2084F80BA7C41D01"
				title: "Kill a Boss Mob"
				type: "advancement"
			}]
			title: "Promotion"
			x: 3.0d
			y: -2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"43AE403E62C96F66"
				"2B712988FC2E66C0"
			]
			dependency_requirement: "one_completed"
			description: [
				"I've no doubt you've noticed your items aren't their normal colors. That, my dear friend, is from the item's &6&oRarity&r"
				"Rarity is important, as it determiens the strength of an item and what kinds of affixes it can have. A good example is that an uncommon and rare item can only have up to 1 gem socket, while higher rarities can have &6&oup to 3&r The rarities are &7Common&r, &2Uncommon&r, &9Rare&r, &5Epic&r, and &6Mythic&r."
				"To increase rarity or craft certain items, you will want to get your hands on some &6&oRarity Materials&r. To do this, you must use Gem Dust to craft a &6&oSalvaging Table&r. Putting an item into the GUI, you will see the amount of Rarity Materials you'll get from salvaging any item. In addition to salvaging items, you can also &o&6salvage gems&r for a much more elegant and efficient method of obtaining it. "
				"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/salvaging-table.png width:308 height:180 align:center}"
			]
			icon: "apotheosis:salvaging_table"
			id: "1935CFAC6173A06F"
			rewards: [{
				amount: 100L
				currency: "eternalcurrencies:ancientcoins"
				id: "423D63B2E64A588F"
				ignore_reward_blocking: true
				type: "eternalcurrencies:currency"
			}]
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "4140A073A74AA6E7"
					item: "apotheosis:salvaging_table"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					count: 3L
